# The Plasma splash screen, for every account on this image — plan/17.
#
# THE SECOND OF TWO FILES, AND NOT THE DECISIVE ONE. What actually selects the splash on a
# Plasma session is /etc/xdg/kdeglobals' [KDE] LookAndFeelPackage — see kdeglobals.in for the
# whole mechanism, and for the bug that taught it to us. The short version: startplasma
# prepends ~/.config/kdedefaults to XDG_CONFIG_DIRS and writes its own ksplashrc in there,
# derived from the Look-and-Feel package id, so anything this file says about Theme is shadowed
# on a real session before the splash is drawn.
#
# It is still shipped, for the reads that do NOT come out of a startplasma session:
#
#   - ksplashqml run by hand, or from an X11 session (startplasma-x11's setupKSplash() reads
#     ksplashrc itself and passes the theme on the command line);
#   - System Settings -> Appearance -> Splash Screen before the session has ever written
#     kdedefaults, which is what the KCM reads to decide which entry is the current one;
#   - Engine, which is checked in three places before anything is drawn (startKSplashViaSystemd(),
#     plasma-session's startup.cpp, and ksplashqml itself) and where a value other than
#     KSplashQML means no splash at all.
#
# ONE FILE PER LAYER, AND NO PER-USER SETUP ANYWHERE IN THIS TREE. KConfig cascades
# $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS underneath ~/.config, so /etc/xdg/ksplashrc is the image's default for any
# user who has not chosen otherwise — the same layer /etc/xdg/kdeglobals, /etc/xdg/baloofilerc
# and the installer medium's /etc/xdg/kscreenlockerrc use. There is no skel copy to keep in
# sync, nothing for Calamares' users module to write, and System Settings still writes a user's
# own choice to ~/.config/ksplashrc, which outranks both this and kdedefaults.
#
# That covers the three populations in one go:
#
#   @LIVE_USER@ on the product image     - reads it from the read-only root
#   @LIVE_USER@ on the installer medium  - same file, same root
#   accounts Calamares creates           - the installed system IS the desktop profile's root
#                                          EROFS, written to disk byte for byte, so this file is
#                                          already there before the account exists
#
# The value is a Plasma/LookAndFeel package id: /usr/share/plasma/look-and-feel/@DISTRO_ID@,
# installed by stage 40 from config/plasma/lookandfeel. Stage 40 asserts that this id, the id in
# that package's metadata.json and the one in /etc/xdg/kdeglobals are all the same string,
# because a disagreement is not an error anywhere at runtime — ksplashqml falls back to Breeze
# and the machine boots to somebody else's logo.
[KSplash]
Engine=KSplashQML
Theme=@DISTRO_ID@
